# stable-diffusion.cpp upstream pin.
#
# Format: two lines. First is a git tag (human-readable, used in
# release notes). Second is the full 40-char commit sha (what build
# scripts actually check out — tags move, shas don't).
#
# Update both together when bumping upstream.
# Verify the commit is reachable from the tag:
#   git -C native/engines/sd-cpp/.upstream fetch --tags
#   git -C native/engines/sd-cpp/.upstream rev-parse <tag>^{commit}
#
# License: MIT (https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp)
upstream=https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp.git
# leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp tags every master commit as
# `master-NNN-<shortsha>`. No semver releases — pinning to the
# latest master-NNN tag IS the stable release.
